{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover","id":264940,"title":"Confused about Cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-24T15:41:50-07:00","id":264940,"title":"Confused about Cover","content":"First off, I'm not bitching about Cover. I'm pretty sure I've got the wrong end of the stick somewhere, but despite how much I leaf through the book I can't 'get' it.<br /> <br /> I like the <i>idea</i> of Cover, I do. I even get most of the mechanics. But the more I read it, the more I come away with the impression that it, well, seems to push players into playing stereotypes, bar people from properly engaging with the game, and really doesn't make it clear the line between the Demon and its Cover. Again, reasonably sure I've got the wrong end of the stick here, and would like some clarification.<br /> <br /> First, the stereotype. This largely comes from the idea of acting too far outside of character of the Cover can lead to Compromise. Individually not really too dramatic an issue, but roll enough you're looking at potential trouble. And sure, it's reasonably cheap/easy to fix (ish, I'll get to that later), but still seems like it's encouraging players, with the risk - not a <i>big</i> risk, true, but certainly possible, and given the consequences if that cosmic roulette wheel comes up 0, concerning - the G-M notices, and diverts Cultists and/or Angels to investigate or cause trouble. So the Demon is encouraged to stay within their Cover. Ok, that's reasonable. Except they make the point that the Cover can't really significantly adapt or grow or change, which means the Demons ability to grow, adapt or change, is horrendously limited. You can tweak around the edges, but that's about as far as you can really go. If your cover is an obese computer programmer, you can dial back on the junk food and maybe go for a walk once in a while, but you can't exactly start going to the gym or start seriously addressing your diet. This means that the Demon needs to change Covers, which they make the point is problematic in a few ways, or you end up static and (for the player at least) boring. This also feeds into the second point.<br /> <br /> Second, engaging with the game. Now, a lot of Demons just kind of keep their metaphysical heads down and try to wiggle by. That's fine. Problem is, that doesn't make for a very interesting game, and is not the impression I've gotten for the expected kind of stories. But in the opening fictions, and in the main text, they indicate that many Demons keep their eyes very closely open for any sign of G-M activities, either to destroy/interfere with it, or to avoid it. Outside of fairly specific Covers, eyeballing a lot of Infrastructure isn't exactly in character. Now you can argue it may not necessarily be dramatically enough <i>out</i> of character to warrant Compromise issues, but see above re: paranoid. And what if the Demon, in scanning the news sites, sees something that warrants further examination? Isn't exactly in-character for, say, a stock trader to go poking around a construction site. The line between in-character and out-of-character-enough seems kind of arbitrary at best, and actively discouraging from a certain type of play at worst, particularly if you're one of the Agendas that do make a habit of acting against the G-M. I get a lot of that is supposed to work off ST-player understanding and co-operation, but the vagueness combined with the general tone seems...problem-inducing. Plus, coming up with multiple Covers seems problematic, since most of the characters stats are informed by the Demons first Cover: what if a Demon who was initially e.g. a stock trader picks up another Cover as e.g. a butcher? Either the stock trader has to pick up a bunch of <i>really</i> out of character skills (with attending butchery classes or whatever probably constituting a Compromise in themselves), or the butcher is going to suddenly suck at his job, and have a lot of really out of character skills. This also feeds into the first point, since the most obvious solution is to only get Covers with a similar set of skills, which leads to stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Finally, the line between the Demon and its Cover. Now, I can see that in some cases it'd be blurry, and that's potentially a lot of fun. But, in a similar vein to the above point, if most of the Demons skills, Merits and Attributes are informed/determined by its first Cover, even when riding other Covers, then the character isn't really a separate entity from its initial Cover, is it? Now, I know the old chestnut, &quot;your character are not their stats&quot;, but come on: stats <i>are</i> a part of the character. They determine dice pools, which determine capability, which determine how they approach a certain situation, which determines how you play them, which determines how you view your character. We've all seen a player with a character who is good at X roll tank a few X rolls in a row, think very carefully about approaching a situation using X skill, even though that is the most logical approach and the dice have just been particularly mean lately. They even say explicitly that Destroyers or Defenders tend to view their Covers as strictly utilitarian while others really identify with them, but there's no mechanical representation of that, and it really seems that there should be. Even the rating of Cover seems to measure how well-integrated into that reality the Demon is, rather than how attached he is to that Cover, and since it determines a lot of your skills and Attributes and more than a few of your social ties, I can't really see how you could easily model your characters relative embracing of their Cover outside of roleplaying, which as I described above can lead to issues with engaging in the game or forging ties with other Demons and interacting with the other players, since there aren't a lot of contexts where a butcher, a priest, a coffee-shop anarchist and a stock trader can regularly meet up and not be arguably well out of character.<br /> <br /> Like I said, <u>I'm not trying to bag on Cover, I'm just trying to understand</u>, and the best way to do that is explain how I perceive it, so people can point out how I'm misunderstanding things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T20:42:54-07:00","id":265146,"title":"","content":"Cover is a morality stat, it's designed just like a morality stat. When Demon's answer their five question's they're answering in relation to that specific cover. Acting out of cover is anything grossly out of cover that would gain great scrutiny from that cover's mortal peers. In the example of your computer tech &quot;What do you mean you don't know what HTML is?&quot; would possibility call for a compromise roll. Remember Demon's are great liars, there's usually away out of those situations. But let's take a Detective, cover breaking would be doing something while on duty that's overly illegal, such as entering someone's house without cause and effect. Cover isn't supposed to be some great mechanical hindrance, it's flavor. And cover's do evolve, check out the Pact system, and read it again. Now one more time. Get it? You can add aspects to your covers by taking them from other people. What a computer genius who's also a body builder, get the Adonis body from a local trainer. The reason why each splat doesn't have a mechanical system for dealing with their cover, because once again, they're just the morality splat to help flavor the game. If your Demon doesn't have a skill that that cover should have, there's an ability all demon's get called &quot;Legend&quot; the point is the challenge, is having to fit in, that's an aspect of being a spy. You are not human, you are not a CEO, but you better start acting like one, slip up too much and the Angels will notice. Learn skills to make it easier, borrow them from the universe as need be.<br /> Your final line of text makes no sense &quot;since there aren't a lot of contexts where a butcher, a priest, a coffee-shop anarchist and a stock trader can regularly meet up and not be arguably well out of character.&quot; People have friend's from all walks of life I'm a catholic housewife whose roleplaying group consists of a Lawyer, a atheist engineer, a Jack in the box manager, and f to m transvestite. People, and their characters will find a reason to bond we do it over roleplaying. Demon's do it over &quot;If you stab me in the back I'm taking you with me&quot; more or less. <br /> <br /> Welcome to the Descent, strap yourself in it's going to be a bumpy ride. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T21:19:39-07:00","id":265948,"title":"","content":"The 4th season premier of Person of Interest is a perfect example of cover in a fictional context. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The Machine now has a rival called Samaritan that acts very much like the God-Machine: always watching, using intermediaries, dupes and agents to actively eliminate threats to its existence. In one scene John grabs the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IdiotBall\" target=\"_blank\">Idiot Ball</a> and has an unsecured conversation that is <i>immediately</i> detected by Samaritan. Even though John's identity holds (he succeeds his compromise roll), Samaritan is now alert that something is up, and sends its agents to investigate (Surveilled condition).<br /> <br /> John is only able to avoid detection when he acts within the confines of his cover identity, albeit he can rig events in his favor (Embeds).</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 09-26-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T22:20:32-07:00","id":265960,"title":"","content":"I think that's a great example! But it might be nice to spoiler it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T00:02:51-07:00","id":266022,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">arkglbsl I had a large thing typed up but then my laptop ate it alkfjklsaf</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Okay, let\u2019s do the (only slightly) shorter version.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, the stereotype. This largely comes from the idea of acting too far outside of character of the Cover can lead to Compromise. Individually not really too dramatic an issue, but roll enough you're looking at potential trouble. And sure, it's reasonably cheap/easy to fix (ish, I'll get to that later), but still seems like it's encouraging players, with the risk - not a <i>big</i> risk, true, but certainly possible, and given the consequences if that cosmic roulette wheel comes up 0, concerning - the G-M notices, and diverts Cultists and/or Angels to investigate or cause trouble. So the Demon is encouraged to stay within their Cover. Ok, that's reasonable. </div> </div> </div>I'lll touch on the stereotype idea at the very end. On Cover ratings: if I\u2019m permitted to quote myself, here\u2019s a </span></span></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/204581-lightening-up-on-cover?p=197154#post197154\"><span style=\"color:#1155cc\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>overlong post</u></span></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> on why I see losing Cover as less of a penalty and more of using a cyclical resource. Note also that with the way the Conditions work and the ability to take Glitches, losing Cover doesn\u2019t automatically reveal you to the G-M, but instead represents a marginal fraying of that identity. Play it smart and keep the strengths and limits of Cover and Cover loss in mind and you\u2019ll be surprised how crazy you can get and still keep your Cover rating relatively intact.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except they make the point that the Cover can't really significantly adapt or grow or change, which means the Demons ability to grow, adapt or change, is horrendously limited. You can tweak around the edges, but that's about as far as you can really go. If your cover is an obese computer programmer, you can dial back on the junk food and maybe go for a walk once in a while, but you can't exactly start going to the gym or start seriously addressing your diet. This means that the Demon needs to change Covers, which they make the point is problematic in a few ways, or you end up static and (for the player at least) boring. This also feeds into the second point. </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re correct in that demons are more restricted in their behavior than regular people, if only because they\u2019re being chased by a near-omniscient creator and the only thing keeping you safe is a static identity that acts as camouflage, that says \u201cI\u2019m normal; I belong\u201d. By and large, though, most people don\u2019t end up changing -that much-, and besides I\u2019d say that with enough time, effort, and even possibly some applications of patch-job pacts or some Compromise rolls one should be able to shift their cover around, even if it\u2019s glacially slow compared to actual people. Real people can have an epiphany and turn their lives around overnight, something that\u2019s not particularly available to the Unchained. Otherwise, it's really up to the ST how hard he should enforce that - but see my next point.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, engaging with the game. Now, a lot of Demons just kind of keep their metaphysical heads down and try to wiggle by. That's fine. Problem is, that doesn't make for a very interesting game, and is not the impression I've gotten for the expected kind of stories. But in the opening fictions, and in the main text, they indicate that many Demons keep their eyes very closely open for any sign of G-M activities, either to destroy/interfere with it, or to avoid it. Outside of fairly specific Covers, eyeballing a lot of Infrastructure isn't exactly in character. Now you can argue it may not necessarily be dramatically enough <i>out</i> of character to warrant Compromise issues, but see above re: paranoid. And what if the Demon, in scanning the news sites, sees something that warrants further examination? Isn't exactly in-character for, say, a stock trader to go poking around a construction site. The line between in-character and out-of-character-enough seems kind of arbitrary at best, and actively discouraging from a certain type of play at worst, particularly if you're one of the Agendas that do make a habit of acting against the G-M. I get a lot of that is supposed to work off ST-player understanding and co-operation, but the vagueness combined with the general tone seems...problem-inducing. </div> </div> </div>The thing to remember about compromise rolls gained by out-of-character behavior is that it\u2019s for when you act <b>grossly</b> out of character. It\u2019s not so much for when you go \u201chuh, I wouldn\u2019t have guessed that\u201d when you find out your boss knows a smattering of French, or when you go \u201cwow, I never would have expected you to do that!\u201d like if the previously fat programmer loses a significant amount of weight. It\u2019s for when your octogenarian pacifist takes down five thugs with moves that would make Jason Bourne blush, or when you find the friendly pastor with a bloody machete and a bunch of chopped up bodies. It\u2019s up to the ST and the player to come to an understanding of course, but in general the guideline I go with is that if it causes a hypothetical bystander to suffer some amount of cognitive dissonance, that\u2019s when I break out the compromise rolls. So with that perspective a stock broker poking around a construction site is weird but it doesn\u2019t make you sit up and go \u201cwait a minute, a stock broker -here-? RED FLAG!\u201d As such, demons can get away with a lot of the basic legwork for their operations before they start risking cover on doing things that they blatantly shouldn\u2019t be doing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, coming up with multiple Covers seems problematic, since most of the characters stats are informed by the Demons first Cover: what if a Demon who was initially e.g. a stock trader picks up another Cover as e.g. a butcher? Either the stock trader has to pick up a bunch of <i>really</i> out of character skills (with attending butchery classes or whatever probably constituting a Compromise in themselves), or the butcher is going to suddenly suck at his job, and have a lot of really out of character skills. This also feeds into the first point, since the most obvious solution is to only get Covers with a similar set of skills, which leads to stereotypes. </div> </div> </div> As miss_minty said, there\u2019s an ability called Legend that all Unchained have that allows a demon access to skills he otherwise has no aptitude with - see page 112-113 in the core book. In Flowers of Hell there\u2019s an Embed that allows you to take a Legend long-term if that\u2019s what you need. The downside is that you get the Imposter Condition, but if you don\u2019t like that (and I don\u2019t) it\u2019s easy enough to toss aside!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, the line between the Demon and its Cover. Now, I can see that in some cases it'd be blurry, and that's potentially a lot of fun. But, in a similar vein to the above point, if most of the Demons skills, Merits and Attributes are informed/determined by its first Cover, even when riding other Covers, then the character isn't really a separate entity from its initial Cover, is it? Now, I know the old chestnut, &quot;your character are not their stats&quot;, but come on: stats <i>are</i> a part of the character. They determine dice pools, which determine capability, which determine how they approach a certain situation, which determines how you play them, which determines how you view your character. We've all seen a player with a character who is good at X roll tank a few X rolls in a row, think very carefully about approaching a situation using X skill, even though that is the most logical approach and the dice have just been particularly mean lately. They even say explicitly that Destroyers or Defenders tend to view their Covers as strictly utilitarian while others really identify with them, but there's no mechanical representation of that, and it really seems that there should be. </div> </div> </div>As you pretty much say, the relationship between Cover and Unchained is a personal one that varies quite a lot. That said, I want to slightly refocus your statement: it\u2019s not their initial cover that determines their abilities, but instead they were designed with a certain cover and mission in mind. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You have to remember that demons are fallen angels, and that angels are built for a specific purpose, not as chameleonic multi-tools; the angel\u2019s assignment (and to a lesser extent the extreme transformation of the Fall) plays an important role in what mixture of skills they have relating to their cover versus what they needed to carry out the God-Machine\u2019s orders. A deep-cover Messenger that\u2019s got its skills mostly tied up in finance and business will probably want to stick to those fields until it branches out; a Destroyer with a flimsy cover built to be a war machine will probably want to stick to covers like cop, war veteran, or bodyguard if he wants his innate talent to be applicable. You might say that this means that a demon is a stereotype, but I\u2019d rather say that Unchained mostly stick to types, and when they don\u2019t they\u2019re operating outside of their comfort zone. On paper this sounds limiting but, well, if different covers allowed demons to do wildly different things, then the Incarnations wouldn\u2019t really work as strong archetypes in my opinion. Put another way: if a player didn\u2019t want to play a combat badass OR experience what it\u2019s like for a war machine to fight against its own nature and try to solve scenarios in ways it\u2019s inexperienced with, why did the player choose to play a Destroyer? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">That said, you\u2019re playing one of reality\u2019s greatest liars, with the ability to pick up skills at a whim, a silver tongue with which to manipulate those around you, and a bunch of powers to bend or break reality to do your bidding. When in doubt, take a high Subterfuge and fake it until you make it! ^_^</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 09-26-2014, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T05:04:50-07:00","id":266093,"title":"","content":"I'm liking Demon enough to toss in a few pennies worth.<br /> <br /> First I'd like to say that after a few sessions, we've noticed at our table that compromise rolls flow like water compared to integrity and breaking points. At the same time, partial transformations, minor transgressions or just being in a high (such as your starting) cover rating simultaneously means you'll 'generally' go unnoticed for a 'long' amount of time... on average. Instead of an occasional check that may or may not break you, you're rolling consistently high pools against a steady erosion. That's the mechanics anyways.<br /> <br /> Regarding stereotypes it might help not to treat your humans as so human from a player's perspective. In most WoD games, you are a human that one day transformed into something else. But not here. You're not playing a human at all, you're playing the bio and/or mechanical eldritch horror that's piloting the human form. People are your cover; that is to say your mundane identities (especially once you can have several), your paper-trail, all those cardboard boxes that say &quot;nothing to see here, move along, no one under here's an ED-209&quot;. You're likely to pick a stereotype the way a mechwarrior picks gauss rifles. You choose to be Bob the comnservative factory worker the way a rogue trader picks a frigate. They're things you put in between you and the god machine, and if you use them really well and treat them really kindly they can last you years and years, but sometimes a Guardian just has to throw &quot;janice the kindly babysitter&quot; in the path of an oncoming hunter angel squadron, Eject or set it to go critical, and hope it can get the flagship out of dock before the smoke clears out.<br /> <br /> In terms of engaging, I find it's a better 'Geist' in several ways. In (again) opposite to most other supernatural splats, Demons hit the ground running (oft quite literally) when it comes to the &quot;of darkness&quot; part of &quot;world&quot;. They may be lacking details, but the challenge is learning to blend in, not expanding their world view. Everything you know is also tainted by probability calculations of God Machine relation and paranoia's at its highest. Anything that happens is &quot;definitely related to you&quot;, whether it is or not. You want to keep your head down, sure, but you want to screw GM almost as hard, and every last ping on your radar comes off to a demon as a missile lock. With the right mindset, anything at all that happens will have their first thoughts be &quot;oh fark it's probably infrastructure&quot;. Demons are semi proactive; you'll get out of your happy hidey hole only when something shows up as a threat, but everything related or connected, everyone you see or meet there should be viewed the way a cynical, not-particularly-good-aligned three-letter-acronym-director does. Always ask yourself &quot;Can I use this and if so How?&quot;. No means eliminate it. Yes? Well, what are you waiting for? That new Gun/Ally/Cover/meatshield/safehouse/falling-angel is waiting for your ability to big-red-button it!<br /> <br /> Leaving the 'hole' though is dirt-easy. You take a trip. You &quot;fortuitously&quot; obtained tickets, or reservations or a free dinner, or you have a meeting, or you were taking a walk when suddenly... If you remember that cover compromising acts are not actually all that rampant and that you're emulating/driving a chassis known for irrationality and spontaneity, You can ever so easily make your way to whatever it is you want to investigate. Or send friends! Or better yet send enemies! Demons have the abilities (listed and explained, no less) to more or less &quot;metagame&quot; on the fly. A demon has its cover laugh or cry the same way a player states his character does so, and often with about as little emotion off your own (or the demon's) face as someone waiting for the bus at five AM. Thinking 'as a player' can, in many ways, actually BE playing the demon in character.<br /> <br /> Your last bit about cover was quite right: The rating is how powerfully ingrained in reality it is - tax returns, medical bills, the intense visceral hatred of that one postman on your route from the time you accidentally backed into his cart... It has nothing to do with whether you'd rather nuke this Rating 9 Hobo than the international supermodel at rank 5, and everything to do with how well built that specific tool is right now.<br /> <br /> Also do go watch person of interest. The two main 'operatives' are spectacular examples of.cold and deadpan killing machines who talk about doing the right thing and how good it makes them feel the way you'd read a vacuum cleaner manual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3948-robotboxes","name":"Robotboxes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T18:24:53-07:00","id":266542,"title":"","content":"So, essentially, you're supposed to sort-of meta-game it, viewing the demon as the player, and the Cover as whatever character he's playing at the moment? That actually makes sense.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd read about Legend, and while I can see the use, I'm not really overly impressed with it covering up holes in your Cover, skill-wise. Say you've got Cover 7, you'd expect 2-odd successes, which translates to 2 skill dots, which translates to less than a single success. I guess if you assume it removes the untrained penalty, it's 1 success-ish. So, sure it's good for the odd patch job, but not the kind of thing you'd want to rely on to fill holes outside your concept. But I guess that's what other demons/not a douche ST are for. Does mean my playing an Amish deacon (Psychopomp Inquisitor) in a game with murders going on may have been unwise, however...<br /> <br /> So patchwork <i>can</i> alter the core concept, albeit very slowly? I got the impression the core concept was inviolable, and you could only really tweak the fringe stuff? That'd actually make things a lot more workable.<br /> <br /> I've seen the first four episodes of Person of Interest, really wasn't impressed with either the writing, the characters or the acting. From what I'm told, the story either doesn't really get going until the second season, but I really couldn't be bothered sitting through yet more episodes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T18:42:11-07:00","id":266554,"title":"","content":"I always took Patchworks as a way to repair any Cover with nice little adds to make a person more 3D (to be removed from the low Cover example in the Core who has a wardrobe filled with the exact same suit over and over again)... If my beginning Cover has dropped I figured a Pact could add a dot or two back on, give a little addition to what makes my Demon's Cover and all is cool... I personally find getting to do Pacts with people IC something rather tough, as unless it's done sneakily without the person's knowledge they're instantly going to know what you're doing with the Pact isn't humanly possible and then the Angels are likely gonna come sniffing around...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T19:14:57-07:00","id":266564,"title":"","content":"It's a &quot;play within a play&quot; affair, yes. You are not playing the human, you are playing the demon that is playing the human. Your demon even, thanks/due to total control, has to actively choose emotes (don't accidentally hit 'dance' instead of 'comfort') and reactions for the human, or he'll just be sitting there, utterly unfazed in his human outfit as everyone around breaks down into a panic or sobbing mess, like he was reading 'my pet goat'.<br /> <br /> Also do not forget to add your attribute dots to that roll! You have just eliminated the untrained penalty and added a dot or two, going from what is most likely a chance die at best to 4-5 dice for skills you are not suited to. You're not 'good' at the skill you're legend-ing, but the difference is otherwise quite massive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3948-robotboxes","user":"Robotboxes","date":". 09-26-2014, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3948-robotboxes","name":"Robotboxes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T07:38:43-07:00","id":266750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=266542#post266542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd read about Legend, and while I can see the use, I'm not really overly impressed with it covering up holes in your Cover, skill-wise. Say you've got Cover 7, you'd expect 2-odd successes, which translates to 2 skill dots, which translates to less than a single success. I guess if you assume it removes the untrained penalty, it's 1 success-ish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus the relevant Attribute.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robotboxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=266093#post266093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons have the abilities (listed and explained, no less) to more or less &quot;metagame&quot; on the fly. A demon has its cover laugh or cry the same way a player states his character does so, and often with about as little emotion off your own (or the demon's) face as someone waiting for the bus at five AM. Thinking 'as a player' can, in many ways, actually BE playing the demon in character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Unless &quot;thinking as a player&quot; leads you to powergame, of course. Then you're a bad person and you should feel bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-27-2014, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T14:15:28-07:00","id":267002,"title":"","content":"Demons themselves should totally be trying to powergame their human character.<br /> Like exchanging someone's &quot;years of co-ed awesome times&quot; for a bus card that'll last them the whole year. Costs you nothing, boosts your cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3948-robotboxes","name":"Robotboxes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T14:32:24-07:00","id":267015,"title":"","content":"If I was a Demon, I'd use the bus card as something to offer as a Pact to a needy person to yoink a year of fun-times from them for my Cover... For a single item my Demon could get a whole bunch of connections to people met, stories where the Demon is now a participant of and of course the Cover boost itself. Though also... If I was a Demon I think a year's bus card is a pretty lame thing to offer for a person's gap year of parties... Of course going by how it's explained, the Pacted human would still remember that gap year, though everyone they met and had times with would think it was my Demon instead of that human. That'd be pretty annoying in some ways if you bumped into a person you met and shared a whole bunch of fun with back then...<br /> <br /> On-Topic; I agree in a way that Demons are kind of hinted at in the Core to stick to a kind of stereotype or risk the Angels sniffing around... Though I'm sure savvy Demons can make sure they're posing in their Cover as someone perfect for what they need and have another being built up or ready to go for something different if they need the change of scenery.<br /> <br /> I don't see too many Demons going into play without Primum 2 so they got room for that extra Cover, whether they're going into the game with it for the extra Merit Dot or they're gonna have fun building the extra up in-game via Pacts etc. That in an essence is 'power gaming', though I see grabbing Primum 2 as a matter of course being something a Demon who wants to survive past their first bust up with powerful Angels or their initial bumps getting to grips with Compromises would see as essential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T17:07:51-07:00","id":267055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=266750#post266750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus the relevant Attribute.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Unless &quot;thinking as a player&quot; leads you to powergame, of course. Then you're a bad person and you should feel bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Badly phrased, possibly: I meant one sucesss <i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> Tangential relevance, just came off a game where if you didn't powergame/minmax, then your ability to affect the story very quickly dropped to zero. That said, that game was pretty awful, but there are reasons to powergame, is my point.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267015#post267015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was a Demon, I'd use the bus card as something to offer as a Pact to a needy person to yoink a year of fun-times from them for my Cover... For a single item my Demon could get a whole bunch of connections to people met, stories where the Demon is now a participant of and of course the Cover boost itself. Though also... If I was a Demon I think a year's bus card is a pretty lame thing to offer for a person's gap year of parties... Of course going by how it's explained, the Pacted human would still remember that gap year, though everyone they met and had times with would think it was my Demon instead of that human. That'd be pretty annoying in some ways if you bumped into a person you met and shared a whole bunch of fun with back then...<br /> <br /> On-Topic; I agree in a way that Demons are kind of hinted at in the Core to stick to a kind of stereotype or risk the Angels sniffing around... Though I'm sure savvy Demons can make sure they're posing in their Cover as someone perfect for what they need and have another being built up or ready to go for something different if they need the change of scenery.<br /> <br /> I don't see too many Demons going into play without Primum 2 so they got room for that extra Cover, whether they're going into the game with it for the extra Merit Dot or they're gonna have fun building the extra up in-game via Pacts etc. That in an essence is 'power gaming', though I see grabbing Primum 2 as a matter of course being something a Demon who wants to survive past their first bust up with powerful Angels or their initial bumps getting to grips with Compromises would see as essential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Current game, not one of the starting characters has Primum 2. Which given that the ST just blew up one of the PCs houses <i>and</i> killed one of his followers in the first session in what was the stupidest possible way, for seemingly no reason, might have been a bad idea.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm probably not the most unbiased individual, since that same guy orchestrated the early ending of a game I was running, and to all appearances was running well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T06:47:38-07:00","id":267383,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267055#post267055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Badly phrased, possibly: I meant one sucesss <i>more</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267055#post267055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=266750#post266750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Unless &quot;thinking as a player&quot; leads you to powergame, of course. Then you're a bad person and you should feel bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangential relevance, just came off a game where if you didn't powergame/minmax, then your ability to affect the story very quickly dropped to zero. That said, that game was pretty awful, but there are reasons to powergame, is my point.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robotboxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267002#post267002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons themselves should totally be trying to powergame their human character.<br /> Like exchanging someone's &quot;years of co-ed awesome times&quot; for a bus card that'll last them the whole year. Costs you nothing, boosts your cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah ...<br /> <br /> The devs' <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/something-other-than-actual-play-balance/\" target=\"_blank\">response</a> to all balance concerns about Demon has been to say any player who might possibly powergame/minmax, even a little, is a jerk and violating the social contract of the game. And, therefore, they will ruin any and every game they take part in - regardless of how balanced or unbalanced the rules are. So there's no point in balancing anything.<br /> <br /> As you may have guessed, this irks me. (I mean, as an ST, I can probably deal with it. But I spend enough time patching things on the fly as it is, you know?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267055#post267055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Current game, not one of the starting characters has Primum 2. Which given that the ST just blew up one of the PCs houses <i>and</i> killed one of his followers in the first session in what was the stupidest possible way, for seemingly no reason, might have been a bad idea.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm probably not the most unbiased individual, since that same guy orchestrated the early ending of a game I was running, and to all appearances was running well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yikes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T07:15:07-07:00","id":267406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267383#post267383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe devs' <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/something-other-than-actual-play-balance/\" target=\"_blank\">response</a> to all balance concerns about Demon has been to say any player who might possibly powergame/minmax, even a little, is a jerk and violating the social contract of the game. And, therefore, they will ruin any and every game they take part in - regardless of how balanced or unbalanced the rules are. So there's no point in balancing anything.<br /> <br /> As you may have guessed, this irks me. (I mean, as an ST, I can probably deal with it. But I spend enough time patching things on the fly as it is, you know?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Foolproofing and the ingenuity of fools is a well-documented complication of rules construction even without getting into the matter of roleplaying games that don't run on rails and dialogue trees. Something my little &quot;research&quot; pet-project has made fairly clear is that just reading thoroughly and comprehensively can usually give you a decent stock of precedent to draw from re: &quot;is it supposed to work like this?&quot; off-the-cuff. The mechanics, while important and useful, are ultimately secondary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:19:03-07:00","id":267415,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree, Satchel.<br /> <br /> You'll note that the example I linked to included much discussion of an ability that allowed a Demon to (covertly and infallibly) kill &quot;boss monsters&quot; and other high-powered characters, pull in nuclear strikes on any location they desired, and in fact perform literally any task it is hypothetically possible to do in the game.<br /> <br /> This was the <i>intended use</i>: that this ability would let you take any action by taking any other, easier action.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would have balanced it by saying that you could only use actions that were of equal difficulty to the target action. But no, apparently you're just supposed to take it as read that using this power to actually <i>achieve</i> anything is &quot;cheating&quot;. Apparently, you can totally kill the President with a hamburger - just not the Destroyer angel sent to take you out.<br /> <br /> But I'm sorry, I'm derailing the thread slightly. It was just off-the-cuff piece of snark, I didn't mean to turn it into me ranting.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, Satchel has pointed out to me in any case that my comments were somewhat unfair. That version of Butterfly Effect was a very early version, and it is in fact balanced much as I suggested in the final draft. That, ultimately, matters much more than the justification for the earlier version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-28-2014, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:15:57-07:00","id":267897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267383#post267383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Yeah ...<br /> <br /> The devs' <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/something-other-than-actual-play-balance/\" target=\"_blank\">response</a> to all balance concerns about Demon has been to say any player who might possibly powergame/minmax, even a little, is a jerk and violating the social contract of the game. And, therefore, they will ruin any and every game they take part in - regardless of how balanced or unbalanced the rules are. So there's no point in balancing anything.<br /> <br /> As you may have guessed, this irks me. (I mean, as an ST, I can probably deal with it. But I spend enough time patching things on the fly as it is, you know?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree entirely, all else being equal. However, when, for example, the ST allows the social-minmaxed character to literally convince a whole city to worship them, and to socialise the automaton followers of another PC to worship them instead, and other less-specialised characters literally never affect the game one iota regardless of what they do, the direction is clear. Is that a badly run game? Oh gods yes. But implicit in that social contract is the ST allowing the players to affect the game world, so if that's got conditions attached to it, then we've already got problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=267406#post267406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Foolproofing and the ingenuity of fools is a well-documented complication of rules construction even without getting into the matter of roleplaying games that don't run on rails and dialogue trees. Something my little &quot;research&quot; pet-project has made fairly clear is that just reading thoroughly and comprehensively can usually give you a decent stock of precedent to draw from re: &quot;is it supposed to work like this?&quot; off-the-cuff. The mechanics, while important and useful, are ultimately secondary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally I'm of the opinion that min-maxers are going to min-max, and the mechanics cannot (and arguably <i>should</i> not try) prevent this, since the more effort you put into trying to stop powergaming inevitably limits player concepts or at least the ease with which they can be realised, and powergamers are ingenious at finding loopholes or making arguments. So, like the tax code built around the idea everyone's a genius accountant out to cheat the system blind (not just be clever, outright cheat), you only end up screwing innocent people to do nothing to the targeted individuals.<br /> <br /> Which I suspect is your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 09-28-2014, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}